        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" value="CHEN NOTATION&lt;br/&gt;Rectangle: entity set. Diamond: relationship set. Oval: attribute. Underline: candidate key.&lt;br/&gt;1 and N beside the entity–relationship connectors denote cardinality ratio (1:N or 1:1), not min–max participation.&lt;br/&gt;Single connector: partial participation. Double connector: total participation. All child entities participate in exactly one parent per relationship.&lt;br/&gt;Parents participate partially: a role may have no users, a user no complaints, a complaint no assignments / feedback / embedding, etc.&lt;br/&gt;Foreign keys appear in the relational schema, not as duplicated ER attributes. Each entity here has an independent surrogate key.&lt;br/&gt;RECEIVES links the assignee (STAFF); CREATES links the assigning actor (ADMIN); RECORDS links the status-change actor.&lt;br/&gt;FEEDBACK and COMPLAINT_EMBEDDINGS map to NOT NULL + UNIQUE complaint_id foreign keys, preserving optional 1:1 extensions.&lt;br/&gt;CATEGORIES also has composite candidate key (department_id, category_name) after mapping. One department is responsible for each category.&lt;br/&gt;Embedding is a pgvector vector-valued attribute; it is not a multivalued attribute. PostgreSQL + pgvector is the proposed storage.&lt;br/&gt;Business rules: one active assignment per complaint; initial history created on submission; feedback by reporter after resolution; role checks and valid transitions enforced separately." style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=18;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#222222;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=15;fontSize=19;fillColor=#f5f5f5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="2850" width="4500" height="280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>